S10.2D-R3.3 effective PID-1 Community contract diagnosis
Date: 2026-09-06
Scope: source-only; no server or public-runtime mutation

Observed contract loss
----------------------
The intended target fragment is
/etc/systemd/system/tu1nz-adult-public-s8-telegram.service. Its ExecStart
contains both existing target arguments:

- --community-contract /etc/tu1nz/adult-commercial-s10-2d-community.json
- --community-copy /etc/tu1nz/adult-commercial-s10-2d-community-copy.json

The inherited source-only drop-in is
/etc/systemd/system/tu1nz-adult-public-s8-telegram.service.d/s10-wms.conf.
It clears ExecStart and supplies a replacement without either Community
argument. systemd drop-in precedence therefore selects the source replacement
as the effective PID-1 command even after the target fragment is installed.
That pre-fix replacement is /usr/bin/env with a bounded PYTHONPATH, the
Application virtual-environment Python and module tu1nz_public_s8.runtime. The
corrected target fragment invokes the existing Application virtual-environment
console entrypoint tu1nz-public-s8-telegram. The working directory remains
/opt/tu1nz_repos/adult-publishing-core in both states.

Root cause
----------
SOURCE_S10_WMS_DROPIN_RESET_EXECSTART_OVERRIDES_TARGET_UNIT

The target controller installed and byte-compared the base fragment but did
not remove the source-only ExecStart override or verify systemd's effective
FragmentPath, DropInPaths and ExecStart before starting the target service.
No wrapper, EnvironmentFile or additional runtime configuration is involved.

Deterministic reproduction
--------------------------
The regression resolves the target fragment followed by the inherited source
drop-in using systemd scalar precedence. The resulting effective command lacks
both Community arguments and is RED as
TARGET_PID1_COMMUNITY_CONTRACT_MISSING.

Minimal correction
------------------
After the existing verified backup and target quiesce, the controller removes
only the source S10 WMS drop-in before daemon-reload. The target base fragment
then becomes the sole effective launch definition. Before any target start, a
fail-closed guard requires the exact fragment path, no S8 drop-ins, chatops
user/group, the canonical Application working directory, no EnvironmentFile,
and both Community arguments in the effective ExecStart. Target verification
repeats this guard.

Source and rollback isolation
-----------------------------
Source preflight pins and verifies the source drop-in hash and confirms that
systemd's effective source command contains no Community argument. The existing
s10-units-before.tar backup includes this drop-in. Rollback extraction restores
it before source verification, so the public S8/S10 fallback remains
Community-disabled.

Canonical Application binding
-----------------------------
The former active target 3617a6c50abeaeb061a8f1b89352178acb6eac94 is an
ancestor of current canonical Application
343a5efe56bebbb0ea82e833f25ef43a91d258dc, tree
85b581a4d47c0098dec2dc78887a89ef40bc33e1. The current commit preserves the
complete S10.2D target and runtime taxonomy and adds only the reviewed
recovery-safe migration 0029 downgrade. The active target and downgrade hash
are rebound to that exact reviewed release. Historical evidence is unchanged.

Safety boundary
---------------
No server synchronization, systemd command, migration, Telegram or BotFather
mutation, Community runtime, real acquisition, Adult media, AVS, payment,
publishing, Controlled Beta or production action is part of R3.3.
